Continuing the audit, I refreshed the consolidated evidence and finalized the report.

**Refreshed `audit/run_all.sh` execution** (`audit/run_all.log`) — the single-command reproduction now reflects the current tests, and every step behaved as documented:

- provenance diff → only nested-module `fuzzy/` differs from the upstream pin;
- `go vet` → clean;
- 7-case malformed-input battery → exactly 3 panics (F1/F2/F3) + 4 graceful controls;
- F1 and F2 direct reproductions → `REPRODUCED ...`;
- benign-flake / durability / consistency tests → all PASS (convergence `maxLag≈11ms`; restart converged; consistency no divergence);
- F1 end-to-end → expected process abort with the `failed to decode configuration` panic.

**Added leadership-transfer churn** to the randomized consistency stress as a distinct fault pattern. Result: `finalLogLen == applied` on both seeds (e.g. 179/179 and 131/131), i.e., every command that succeeded was applied exactly once on every node, no divergence — with `failed` applies being the expected leadership-loss/timeout responses. I recorded the run-to-run variance honestly rather than quoting a single fixed number.

**Standing result (unchanged in substance):** three concrete, reproducible defects — F1 (`InstallSnapshot.Configuration`), F2 (unknown `LogType`), F3 (`LogConfiguration.Data`) — one localized class of RPC-reachable, unauthenticated, remote-crash defects with no `recover()` in the RPC main loop, and with the analogous control paths proving the fragility is specific to exactly three call sites. All inherited from upstream v1.7.3 (tree byte-identical to the release; nothing claimed as injected). Report is organized with expected-behavior/basis, affected code, necessary conditions, actual behavior, executed-vs-source distinctions, checked alternatives, and severity caveats.

Report: [report.md](/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/baseline/runs/2026-10-09_08-06-10-hashicorp_raft-baseline/work/report.md) (18 headings, 13 artifacts under `work/audit/`). Remaining gaps unchanged and documented: the ~15 TCP/loopback test groups need the private-loopback `isolated_exec`, and `fuzzy/`/`raft-compat/` have no offline reference or runnable dependencies.
